# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the value.
# `.env.local` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed or shipped in a zip.
#
# WHY YOU NEED THIS
# -----------------
# Most of the app runs on the publishable key in `.env`, protected by Row Level
# Security. A few Super Admin operations cannot: creating a restaurant owner's
# login calls the Auth Admin API, which only the service_role key may use.
#
# Without it you get:
#   "TAIMOOR created, but the owner account could not be made:
#    Missing server-side Supabase configuration: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"
#
# The restaurant IS created; only its owner login is missing.
#
# WHERE TO GET IT
# ---------------
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys -> service_role -> Reveal
#
# THE RULE
# --------
# Never give this a VITE_ prefix. Vite inlines VITE_* into the browser bundle,
# and this key bypasses RLS — in a browser it exposes every tenant's data to
# anyone who opens devtools. src/lib/supabase.ts refuses to start if it detects
# a secret key on the client, but do not rely on that catching it.

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
